From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:46:56 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 133/297] Meridian: the command bar finds Settings

Like "search everywhere" in an editor: typed in the command bar, the name
of a section of Settings ("ai"), of an option in one ("api keys", "block
ads", "search engine") or of a page of Chromium's settings ("privacy",
"site settings") is offered with where it is. Picking it opens Meridian's
Settings at that section with the option scrolled into sight and marked for
a moment, or the Chromium page in a tab.

The entries are a list of their own (settings_index.ts) beside the
features: up to three features, then up to three settings. A setting named
in full goes first and is picked for Return ("ai": Settings' AI, before
Chat); named by a word only it is offered but not picked, so "privacy" and
Return still searches.

Settings opened this way takes the keys, so Escape closes it (the command
bar hands them to the page as it closes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
